{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041907-what-is-the-actual-range-of-outward-and-inward-eye","id":1041907,"title":"What is the actual range of Outward and Inward Eye?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-01T10:35:04-08:00","id":1041907,"title":"What is the actual range of Outward and Inward Eye?","content":"So! Outward and Inward Eye functions so that the Mage's hearing and vision count as originating from every point and orientation that they could normally see and hear, without regards to distance or barriers.<br /> <br /> Stars are visible, and they are billions of lightyears away.<br /> <br /> What is the actual limitation on what this spell lets you see? I doubt its intent is for a Space 1 Mage to be automatically aware of everything that happens within 2.9 billion lightyears.<br /> <br /> Also, if you use the reach effect for your senses to extend through Scrying Windows, and you have an open scrying window, do you need one reach or two reach to affect something on the other side? [Its a video, but your natural senses are extended through it more literally. And OaIE explicitly allows sensory range]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:48:50-08:00","id":1041916,"title":"","content":"Visual resolution is still based on actual relative position.<br /> <br /> Casting through a scrying window explicitly counts as remote casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:18:11-08:00","id":1041954,"title":"","content":"It's a sifficult effect to word properly, but I think the intent is that you can percieve everything up until the horizon that's not in some completely sealed box or room (even if you could interpret it to bend over there too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:02:10-08:00","id":1041978,"title":"","content":"I agree with Satchel the relevant bit is this: <br /> <br /> 'She cannot perceive things farther away than her normal perceptions might allow, nor can she see through darkness. In essence, it\u2019s as though everything happening around her were spread out on a flat plain, bereft of obstruction.'<br /> <br /> It allows you to ignore obstacles, but not 'zoom in'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:02:12-08:00","id":1041979,"title":"","content":"Even when you change your viewpoint via the spell you can still only see it as well as you could from your original position. It's more like zooming in on an image and continuing to lose fidelity because the camera can only pick up so many pixels instead of going fractal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:06:25-08:00","id":1041984,"title":"","content":"So, essentially the normal human visual range based on the curvature of the earth which is 1 mile give or take depending on where you are standing. If you are on the ground level, it would be 1 mile. If you are on top of a really high mountain, according to the equation for distance viewable it is 148 miles. Of course, I think you still see with the same vision as normal meaning that guy looks 2 cm high nearly a mile away, but maybe with some Forces you could enhance your vision.<br /> <br /> You can check this link here to get a better understanding: <a href=\"http://www.davidsenesac.com/Information/line_of_sight.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.davidsenesac.com/Informat..._of_sight.html</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:41:46-08:00","id":1042086,"title":"","content":"Basically your vision bends, so you can see around corners, through keyholes and so forth.<br /> If the winding path of your vision has to go through about 500m before it can see someone who's standing 5 meters away on the other side of a wall, then you'll see him as if from 500m away.<br /> So you can only see so far as your eyesight normally would, though you can see everyone within a winding bendy path of that sight.<br /> <br /> So add in Life for some Eagle Eyes, and you're in the clear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:52:51-08:00","id":1042092,"title":"","content":"Aye the wording on that spell is difficult. The main issue, I think, that keeps on cropping up is that, grammatically, to say that your senses are originating FROM a point is to say that it is as if you are THERE at that point. If you delete that portion from the description, the spell reads much, MUCH more closely to what the author intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:26:55-08:00","id":1042276,"title":"","content":"Yep, it's as others have said. You see everything around you as if you had a direct, unobstructed line of sight to it <i>from your current position</i>. It doesn't let you see further than you normally could, or see in the dark or any other manner of viewing that you couldn't perceive already, but it allows you to see everything as if you were looking directly at it with nothing in between you and it.<br /> <br /> So you could probably see the figure of a person a mile away through a city block worth of stuff, but without additional magic you probably wouldn't be able to tell <i>who </i>it was or make out very many specific details about said person. You could see through the door into the next room, but if all the lights were off in there, you'd only be able to see in it as well as you normally would if you were to look into a room that dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}